Source: homelab-database
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-database
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, postgresql, postgresql-client, homelab-common
Recommends: homelab-agent
Suggests: patroni, etcd-server, etcd-client, python3-etcd, python3-dnspython, keepalived
Description: PostgreSQL provisioning substrate for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Installs/configures PostgreSQL itself and idempotently creates the one
 shared `homelab` database every feature's own narrow schema lives
 inside. The split-role bootstrap tool for provisioning an individual
 feature's own roles/schema (homelab-bootstrap-app-role) lives in
 homelab-common instead of here, so any feature host can depend on the
 lightweight client tool without this whole package (and a full local
 Postgres server) coming along with it. Needs a hard Depends on
 homelab-common itself too, same reasoning as homelab-pgbouncer's own
 identical fix: a remote feature host's role-bootstrap SSHes INTO this
 host and runs that tool locally here, which needs the binary present
 on THIS side, not just the caller's.

Package: homelab-database-ha
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         homelab-database (= ${source:Version}),
         patroni,
         etcd-server,
         etcd-client,
         python3-etcd,
         python3-dnspython,
         keepalived
Description: Install-time Patroni/etcd/keepalived HA for homelab-database
 Turns a homelab-database host into a Patroni-managed PostgreSQL cluster
 member at install time, instead of as a manual after-the-fact step.
 Pulls the HA stack (patroni + a 3-node-capable etcd + keepalived) as
 hard dependencies -- so they are present before this package's postinst
 runs -- then drives homelab-database-ha-bootstrap (shipped by
 homelab-database) from debconf answers: a fresh install comes up HA-ready
 even as a single-node (one-member) cluster that is trivially extended by
 installing this package on the other members with the same member list.
 The database VIP (keepalived) follows the Patroni leader so pgbouncer and
 apps reach the current primary transparently across failovers. Install
 plain homelab-database instead for a standalone (non-HA) node.
